he route applies reqToken() and then reqAdmin(). reqAdmin requires repository-admin or site-admin status and returns forbidden when both are absent, so the stated authenticated issue writer is rejected before LockIssue runs. The handler's later issue/pull-request write check is therefore not reached in this scenario, and the unlocked-issue lock mutation is not reached. Thus the supplied source enforces the accepted deny-nonadmin policy; full token scope and issue-write permission do not bypass the earlier administrator gate. The route/handler source does not establish any repository-wide or deployment-wide completeness claim.","facts":[{"id":"entry-put-lock","kind":"entry","statement":"The declared lock route binds PUT to the issue-lock handler and applies token authentication followed by the administrator guard.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-abc290f763b410ea","startLine":16,"endLine":20}]},{"id":"principal-admin-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"The route's administrator guard evaluates the authenticated context for repository-administrator or site-administrator status.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-abc290f763b410ea","startLine":4,"endLine":8}]},{"id":"resource-issue-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"The handler resolves the addressed issue using the repository context and the integer path index before authorization of the lock operation.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-ed35041e326128c5","startLine":42,"endLine":47}]},{"id":"control-admin-first","kind":"control","statement":"When neither repository-admin nor site-admin status is present, reqAdmin emits HTTP 403 and returns, making this the decisive first authorization gate.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-abc290f763b410ea","startLine":4,"endLine":11}]},{"id":"control-issue-write","kind":"control","statement":"If execution reaches the handler, it separately requires permission to write issues or pull requests and otherwise emits HTTP 403.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-ed35041e326128c5","startLine":49,"endLine":52}]},{"id":"condition-unlocked","kind":"condition","statement":"The lock effect is conditional on the issue not already being locked.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-ed35041e326128c5","startLine":54,"endLine":57}]},{"id":"effect-lock-mutation","kind":"effect","statement":"The protected effect constructs lock options with the current user and issue, then invokes the issue lock operation; this effect occurs only after the preceding gates return successfully.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-ed35041e326128c5","startLine":54,"endLine":67}]}],"decisiveMissingFacts":[],"suggestedObservations":[]}]}}],"tokens":{"input":2432,"output":940,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0},"costUsd":null,"durationMs":34154.467000000004,"stopReason":"tool_use"},"schemaValidation":{"valid":true,"diagnostics":[]},"endedAt":"2026-09-27T13:01:40.389Z"}}
